mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;background:rgb(217,217,217);">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:12.0000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">4.教学内容及进度安排</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">/Course Content & Schedule</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:12.0000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">（</font></span><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Courier New';font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">按照教学周编排，应包含每节课教学内容及教学目标，如有作业及考核要求，请一并列明）</font></span><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:12.0000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:176.7000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>一、Theoretical Course Teaching Plan</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>1</strong><strong><sup>st</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week </strong><strong>Preface, clinical anatomy and physiology of ear, trauma of ear, disease of auricle</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Anatomy of the external, middle and internal ear. Physiology of hearing and equilibrium.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Examination of the external ear and tympanic membrane. Investigation of Eustachian tube function. Tuning-fork test, pure tone audiometry, acoustic impedance, auditory brainstem response audiometry and vestibular function test.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The clinical manifestations and management of injury of the tympanic membrane. The clinical manifestations and management of fracture of the temporal bone.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>2</strong><strong><sup>nd</sup></strong><strong>Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Acute otitis media, chronic otitis media, middle ear cholesteatoma</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, pathology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, differential diagnosis and treatment of acute and chronic otitis media and cholesteatoma.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>3</strong><strong><sup>rd</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week </strong><strong>Examination of hearing, otosclerosis, prevention and therapy of deafness</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, differential diagnosis and treatment of otosclerosis.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, clinical features, diagnosis, treatment and prevention of conductive, sensorineural and mixed deafness.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>4</strong><strong><sup>th </sup></strong><strong>Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Examination of vestibular function, Meniere disease, ear neoplasms</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, pathology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, differential diagnosis and treatment of Ménière disease</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of papilloma of the external auditory canal, cancer of the middle ear and tumors of lateral skull base and internal auditory canal.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>5</strong><strong><sup>th</sup></strong><strong>Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Otogenic complication, facial paralysis</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The diagnosis and management of otogenic complication. T</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">he etiology, pathophysiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of peripheral facial paralysis.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>6</strong><strong><sup>th</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Clinical anatomy and physiology of the nose and paranasal sinuses, rhinitis</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Anatomical structures of external nose, nasal cavity and paranasal sinus. Distribution of blood vessels, nerves and lymph nodes in nasal cavity.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Physiological functions of the nasal cavity. The diagnosis and management of rhinitis.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>7</strong><strong><sup>th</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Trauma of nose, epistaxis, disease of nasal septum, foreign body in the nose</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The diagnosis and management algorithm of the fracture of nasal bone and paranasal sinus. The clinical manifestations and treatment of deviation of the nasal septum.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology and treatment of epistaxis.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The diagnosis and treatment of foreign bodies in nasal cavity and paranasal sinus.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>8</strong><strong><sup>th</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Rhinosinusitis, nasal and skull base neoplasms</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of the acute and chronic rhinosinusitis.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The clinical manifestations and treatment of nasal papilloma. The clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of malignant tumors of nasal cavity and paranasal sinus.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>9</strong><strong><sup>th</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Clinical anatomy of pharynx, tonsillitis, adenoidal hypertrophy, periamygdalitis, pharyngeal abscess</strong><strong>,</strong><strong>&nbsp;OSAHS, pharyngeal neoplasms</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Composition of the pharynx. Space of the pharynx: retropharyngeal and parapharyngeal space. Lymph nodes, blood vessels and nerves of the pharynx. Physiological functions of the pharynx.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, clinical manifestations, complications, diagnosis, differential diagnosis and treatment of acute and chronic tonsillitis. The indication and contraindication of tonsillectomy.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of adenoidal hypertrophy. The etiology, pathology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, differential diagnosis and treatment of peritonsillar abscess.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, pathology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of retropharyngeal abscess. The etiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of parapharyngeal abscess.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of OSAHS, nasopharyngeal fibroangioma and nasopharyngeal carcinoma.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>10</strong><strong><sup>th</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Clinical anatomy of the trachea, bronchi and esophagus, foreign bodies in the trachea and bronchi, foreign bodies in the esophagus</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Anatomical features and clinical significance of principal bronchi. The clinical significance of the four physiological strictures of the esophagus.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, sorts, location, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of foreign bodies in trachea and bronchi.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of foreign bodies of the esophagus. Complications of foreign bodies of the esophagus.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>11</strong><strong><sup>th</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Clinical anatomy and physiology of larynx, injuries of larynx, disease of laryngeal nerves, inflammation of larynx</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Cartilage framework of the larynx. Composition of laryngeal muscles. Structure of laryngeal cavity: supraglottic, glottic and infraglottic portion. Blood vessels, nerves and lymph nodes of the larynx. Anatomical features and clinical significance of the larynx in children. Physiological functions of the larynx: respiration, phonation, protection and holding breath.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, clinical manifestations and treatment of contusion of the larynx. The etiology, clinical manifestations and treatment of cutting injury of the larynx. The etiology, clinical manifestations and treatment of scald, burning injury of the larynx. The etiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of stenosis of the larynx.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of hysterical aphonia. The etiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of laryngeal paralysis.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, pathology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of acute epiglottitis. The etiology, pathology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of laryngitis. The clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of acute laryngitis in children.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of vocal nodules. The clinical manifestations, diagnosis and treatment of polyp of vocal cord.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>12</strong><strong><sup>th</sup></strong><strong>&nbsp;Week</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Laryngeal obstruction, tracheotomy, laryngeal neoplasms</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, differential diagnosis and treatment of laryngeal obstruction.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The clinical anatomy of trachea. Surgical indication and procedures. Postoperative care and complications.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The etiology, pathology, clinical manifestations and treatment of laryngeal papilloma.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The diagnosis and treatment of other benign tumors of the larynx (hemangioma, fibroma and neurofibroma). The etiology, pathology, staging, clinical manifestations, metastasis, diagnosis, differential diagnosis and treatment of laryngeal carcinoma.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">二、Demonstration Course Teaching Plan</span></strong></p>
<p><strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Lesson 1: </span></strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Anatomy and Physiology of the Ear, Nose, and Throat</span><strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><br>Lesson 2: </span></strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Otolaryngological Examination and Symptomatology</span><strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><br>Lesson 3: </span></strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Otolaryngology Diseases part&nbsp; I (Otology)</span><strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><br>Lesson 4: </span></strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Otolaryngology Diseases part II (Rhinology)</span><strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><br>Lesson 5: </span></strong><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Otolaryngology Diseases part III (Throat + Head and Neck)</span></p></font></span><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
